  "worked_solution": "Two vectors are equal if and only if they lie on parallel lines and have both the same magnitude and the same direction.\n\nThe vectors $b$ and $d$ have opposite directions, hence, $b\\ne d.$ \n\nOn the other hand, $c\\ne b$ and $c\\ne d$ because they are not parallel.\n\nSo, the only pair of equal vectors is $a=e.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/853590f28737bd24abc5c02907f1d1cdb67f5c46a7d10ddc86bd90a1e7435418.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
